COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.performance_kpi_target.target_name IS 'Human-readable name or label for this KPI target record, used for identification and reporting purposes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.performance_kpi_target.target_period_end_date IS 'The end date of the period for which this KPI target is applicable. Used for time-bound performance measurement and pacing analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.performance_kpi_target.target_period_start_date IS 'The start date of the period for which this KPI target is applicable. Used for time-bound performance measurement and pacing analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.performance_kpi_target.target_source IS 'The origin or basis for this KPI target. Insertion Order (IO) commitment represents contractual obligation, client brief represents client expectation, internal benchmark represents agency standard, historical average represents past performance baseline.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.performance_kpi_target.target_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the KPI target. Draft = under definition, active = in measurement period, suspended = temporarily paused, achieved = target met, missed = target not met, expired = measurement period ended.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.performance_kpi_target.target_unit IS 'The unit of measure for the target value. Currency for cost-based KPIs (CPM, CPC, CPA), percentage for rate-based KPIs (CTR, VTR, viewability_rate), ratio for ROAS, points for GRP/TRP, count for absolute metrics.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.performance_kpi_target.target_value IS 'The numeric target value for the specified KPI. Interpretation depends on kpi_type (e.g., dollar amount for CPM/CPC/CPA, percentage for CTR/VTR/viewability_rate, ratio for ROAS, points for GRP/TRP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.performance_kpi_target.tolerance_percentage IS 'Acceptable variance percentage from the target value before triggering alerts or escalations. For example, 10.00 means ±10% from target is acceptable. Used for pacing alerts and performance monitoring.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.performance_kpi_target.upper_threshold IS 'The maximum acceptable value for this KPI (relevant for cost-based metrics where exceeding target is negative). Performance above this threshold triggers alerts. Calculated as target_value plus tolerance band or set explicitly.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.performance_kpi_target.viewability_standard IS 'The viewability measurement standard applied for viewability_rate KPI targets. MRC standard = 50% of pixels in view for 1 second (display) or 2 seconds (video). GroupM may have stricter requirements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.performance_kpi_target.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.performance_kpi_target.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.performance_kpi_target.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.performance_kpi_target.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_by.';

COMMENT ON TABLE performance.tracking_pixel IS 'Master record and complete operational event log for each tracking pixel or conversion tag deployed on advertiser web properties, app environments, or landing pages. Header section stores pixel definition: name, type (impression tracker, click tracker, conversion tag, retargeting pixel, audience pixel), implementation method (JavaScript, image pixel, server-to-server), firing rules, consent flags, and deployment status. Detail section stores the complete fire event history: individual fire timestamps, firing URL, user agent, IP hash (GDPR-compliant), referrer URL, custom parameters passed, fire status (success/blocked/timeout), and error details. Single source of truth for all pixel infrastructure configuration AND raw fire event data. Serves as the unified measurement infrastructure registry, pixel health monitoring source, and raw fire event stream for conversion deduplication and data quality validation. Supports GDPR/CCPA consent compliance workflows and tag governance audits.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.tracking_pixel_id IS 'Unique identifier for the tracking pixel or conversion tag record. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.ad_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.ad. Business justification: Ad-level pixel assignment is standard for impression and click tracking tags embedded in specific ad units. Trafficking teams assign view_tracker_url and impression_tracker_url pixels to individual ad LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.ad.ad_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the advertiser client whose property or campaign this pixel is deployed on. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.advertiser.advertiser_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.agency_relationship_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.agency_relationship. Business justification: Pixel deployment is governed by the agency relationship agreement — consent requirements, data sharing rights, and pixel ownership are defined per AOR. Pixel audits and agency transitions require know LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.agency_relationship.agency_relationship_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.asset_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.asset. Business justification: Tracking pixels are deployed within specific creative assets for conversion tracking. Trafficking and analytics teams need this link to validate pixel deployment, troubleshoot firing issues, and recon LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.asset.asset_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: Tracking pixels are deployed for brand-specific conversion measurement. Brand managers need to audit which pixels are active for their brands, manage brand-specific conversion definitions, and ensure LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.brand.brand_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the advertising campaign this pixel is associated with for measurement purposes. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.creative_deliverable_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.creative_deliverable. Business justification: Tracking pixels are deployed against specific creative deliverables for conversion and interaction tracking. Ad ops teams associate pixels with deliverables during trafficking — a direct operational d LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.creative_deliverable.creative_deliverable_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.flight_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.flight. Business justification: Pixels are deployed with flight-scoped lookback windows to capture conversions within specific flight periods. Flight-level pixel deployment is standard practice for phased campaigns where each flight LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.flight.flight_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.line_item_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.line_item. Business justification: Line-item-level pixel deployment enables granular conversion attribution for programmatic and direct line items. Ad ops assigns specific pixels to line items to measure post-click and post-view conver LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.line_item.line_item_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.media_placement_id IS 'Reference to the specific media placement or ad unit this pixel is tracking. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.media_placement.media_placement_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.segment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.segment. Business justification: Pixel-to-segment mapping for retargeting: tracking pixels are deployed to populate specific audience segments (e.g., site-visitor retargeting pixel feeds a ''cart abandoner'' segment). This link is requ LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.segment.segment_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: SOWs define measurement and tracking requirements as contractual deliverables. Linking pixels to SOWs enables scope validation, ensures deployed tracking matches contracted specifications, and support LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sow.sow_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Tracking pixels are often provided by third-party tag management or analytics vendors (Google Tag Manager, Tealium, Adobe). Required for troubleshooting pixel fires, SLA management, vendor consolidati LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.tech_partner_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.tech_partner. Business justification: Pixels are issued by tech partners (e.g., CM360 Floodlight, DSP conversion tags). Linking pixel to originating tech partner is required for data governance audits, tech stack rationalization, and GDPR LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.tech_partner.tech_partner_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.trafficking_instruction_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.trafficking_instruction. Business justification: Trafficking instructions specify pixel deployment (impression_tracking_pixel_url, vast_tag_url, viewability_tag_url). Pixels are created and deployed as part of trafficking instructions. A trafficking LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.trafficking_instruction.trafficking_instruction_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.browser_name IS 'Name of the web browser in which the pixel fired, parsed from the user agent string.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.consent_category IS 'Privacy consent category under which this pixel operates, determining when it may fire based on user consent preferences.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.consent_required_flag IS 'Indicates whether user consent is required before the pixel can fire, per privacy regulations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.conversion_currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for the conversion value.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.conversion_value IS 'Monetary value associated with a conversion event tracked by this pixel, used for ROAS calculation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.custom_parameters IS 'Additional key-value pairs or query string parameters passed with the pixel fire for custom tracking dimensions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.deduplication_key IS 'Unique identifier used to prevent duplicate counting of the same conversion event across multiple pixels or platforms.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.deployment_environment IS 'The digital environment or platform type where the pixel is implemented.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.deployment_status IS 'Current operational status of the tracking pixel in the measurement infrastructure.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.deployment_url IS 'The advertiser web page, app screen, or landing page URL where this pixel is deployed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.device_type IS 'Classification of the device on which the pixel fired, derived from user agent analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.error_code IS 'Technical error code returned when a pixel fire fails, used for troubleshooting and data quality monitoring.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.error_message IS 'Human-readable description of the error that occurred during pixel fire, providing diagnostic detail.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.fire_status IS 'Outcome status of the pixel fire attempt, indicating whether the tracking event was successfully recorded.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.fire_timestamp IS 'Exact date and time when the pixel fire event occurred, representing the principal business event for this tracking record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.firing_rule IS 'Business logic or condition that determines when the pixel should fire (e.g., page load, button click, form submission, time on page).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.geo_city IS 'City derived from IP geolocation at time of pixel fire.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.geo_country_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 country code derived from IP geolocation at time of pixel fire.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.geo_region IS 'State, province, or region derived from IP geolocation at time of pixel fire.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.implementation_method IS 'Technical method used to deploy and fire the tracking pixel on the target property.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.ip_address_hash IS 'One-way cryptographic hash of the user IP address, stored for fraud detection and geographic analysis while maintaining GDPR compliance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.lookback_window_days IS 'Number of days after an ad interaction during which a conversion can be attributed to that interaction.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.notes IS 'Free-form text field for additional comments, implementation instructions, or troubleshooting notes related to this pixel.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.operating_system IS 'Operating system of the device on which the pixel fired, parsed from the user agent string.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.pixel_code IS 'Unique external code or identifier for the pixel used in trafficking and reporting systems.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.pixel_name IS 'Human-readable name assigned to the tracking pixel for identification and management purposes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.pixel_type IS 'Classification of the tracking pixel based on its measurement purpose and firing trigger.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.pixel_url IS 'Full URL endpoint that the pixel fires to when triggered, including protocol and domain.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.referrer_url IS 'The URL of the page that referred the user to the page where the pixel fired, used for traffic source analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.user_agent IS 'Browser or application user agent string captured at the time of pixel fire, used for device and browser classification.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable. MVM column: created_by_user.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.tracking_pixel.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_by_user.';

COMMENT ON TABLE performance.click_event IS 'Raw click interaction event record capturing each user click on a served ad unit. Stores click timestamp, placement identifier, creative identifier, redirect URL, device fingerprint, and click validation status (invalid traffic / IVT flags per TAG/MRC standards). Source of CPC billing actuals and CTR computation inputs. Distinct from impression_event: represents a user-initiated interaction, not a passive delivery.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.click_event_id IS 'Unique identifier for each click event record. Primary key for the click event entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.ad_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.ad. Business justification: Ad-level click attribution is essential for creative A/B testing and rotation weight optimization. Creative strategists compare click rates across ad variants to determine winning creatives. creative_ LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.ad.ad_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.asset_id IS 'Reference to the creative asset that was clicked. Identifies the specific ad unit, banner, video, or interactive element that received the user interaction. LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.asset.asset_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the advertising campaign under which this click occurred. Enables campaign-level click aggregation and performance analysis. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.contract_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_insertion_order. Business justification: CPC-based IOs require click-level tracking for budget consumption and invoice reconciliation. Enables automated billing validation against contracted click rates and caps. Essential for performance-ba LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_insertion_order.contract_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.flight_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.flight. Business justification: Flight-level CTR and click volume reporting is a standard campaign performance dashboard metric. Media planners evaluate click performance per flight to reallocate budget across flights mid-campaign. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.flight.flight_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.impression_event_id IS 'Reference to the parent impression event that was served before this click occurred. Links click to the originating ad delivery event. LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.impression_event.impression_event_id (not enforced: partitioned target).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.line_item_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.line_item. Business justification: Line-item CTR is a fundamental optimization metric in programmatic and direct buying. Traders use line-item click data to adjust bids, targeting, and creative rotation. No existing FK on click_event t LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.line_item.line_item_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.media_placement_id IS 'Reference to the media placement where the clicked ad was served. Identifies the specific inventory position and publisher context. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.media_placement.media_placement_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.publisher_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.publisher. Business justification: Publisher-level click-through rate reporting is a standard ad ops function. Agencies track CTR by publisher for inventory quality assessment and vendor scorecards. click_event has no publisher_id; joi LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.publisher.publisher_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.segment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.segment. Business justification: Clicks occur within targeted segments - critical for segment-level CTR analysis, engagement measurement, and audience quality scoring. Enables advertisers to identify high-performing segments and opti LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.segment.segment_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.tracking_pixel_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.tracking_pixel. Business justification: click_event currently has a `tracking_pixel_fired_flag` BOOLEAN column indicating whether a tracking pixel fired on this click, but no FK to identify WHICH pixel fired. Adding tracking_pixel_id as a n';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.ad_server_name IS 'The name or identifier of the ad server that recorded and tracked this click event (e.g., Google Campaign Manager 360, Sizmek, Flashtalking). Used for data reconciliation and discrepancy analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.attribution_window_hours IS 'The number of hours after the click during which a conversion can be attributed to this click event. Typically set at campaign or advertiser level (e.g., 24, 72, 168 hours).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.billing_status IS 'Indicates whether this click event is billable under the cost-per-click (CPC) pricing model. Non-billable clicks include invalid traffic, duplicate clicks, and clicks outside contracted parameters.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.click_fraud_score IS 'Numeric fraud risk score assigned by the invalid traffic detection system, typically ranging from 0 (legitimate) to 100 (high fraud risk). Used for sophisticated IVT filtering and billing dispute resolution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.click_interaction_type IS 'The type of user interaction that triggered the click event. Distinguishes between standard clicks, video overlay clicks, expandable ad interactions, and mobile gestures. Code set: ref.click_interaction_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.click_latency_ms IS 'Time elapsed in milliseconds between the impression render and the click event. Used to detect rapid-fire bot clicks and analyze user engagement timing patterns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.click_position_x IS 'Horizontal pixel coordinate of the click within the ad unit. Used for heatmap analysis and creative engagement optimization.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.click_position_y IS 'Vertical pixel coordinate of the click within the ad unit. Used for heatmap analysis and creative engagement optimization.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.click_redirect_url IS 'The destination URL to which the user was redirected after clicking the ad. May include tracking parameters, campaign identifiers, and attribution tokens.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.click_source_platform IS 'The platform or channel through which the click was delivered. Distinguishes between web, mobile app, connected TV (CTV), digital out-of-home (DOOH), and other channels. Code set: ref.click_source_platform.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.click_timestamp IS 'Precise date and time when the user clicked the ad unit, captured in UTC. Primary business event timestamp for click-through rate (CTR) calculation and time-series analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.click_validation_status IS 'Validation status indicating whether the click is considered legitimate traffic or flagged as invalid per TAG (Trustworthy Accountability Group) and MRC (Media Rating Council) invalid traffic (IVT) detection standards. Determines billability for cost-per-click (CPC) campaigns. Code set: ref.click_validation_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.conversion_attributed_flag IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether this click event was later attributed to a conversion event within the attribution window. Used for click-to-conversion analysis and return on ad spend (ROAS) calculation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.cpc_rate IS 'The contracted cost per click rate for this event in the campaign currency. Used to calculate click-level revenue and cost-per-acquisition (CPA) metrics.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for the CPC rate and billing amounts. Supports multi-currency campaign reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.data_source_system IS 'The operational system or platform that generated this click event record (e.g., Google Campaign Manager 360, The Trade Desk, Mediaocean Prisma). Used for data lineage tracking and multi-source reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.device_fingerprint IS 'Hashed or anonymized device identifier derived from browser characteristics, IP address, user agent, and other signals. Used for fraud detection, frequency capping, and cross-session attribution without relying on cookies.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.device_type IS 'Category of device on which the click occurred. Supports device-level performance segmentation and cross-device attribution analysis. Code set: ref.device_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.geographic_city IS 'City or metropolitan area where the click occurred, derived from IP geolocation. Supports hyper-local campaign performance analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.geographic_country_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 country code representing the geographic location of the click based on IP geolocation. Supports geo-targeting validation and regional performance analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.geographic_region IS 'State, province, or administrative region where the click occurred, derived from IP geolocation. Enables sub-national geographic performance segmentation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.ip_address IS 'The IP address from which the click originated. Used for geographic targeting validation, fraud detection, and datacenter traffic filtering. May be anonymized or hashed per GDPR and CCPA requirements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.ivt_detection_method IS 'The method or layer at which invalid traffic detection was applied: general IVT (GIVT) for automated bot detection, sophisticated IVT (SIVT) for advanced fraud analysis, or manual review.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.referrer_url IS 'The URL of the page or application context where the ad was displayed and clicked. Used for contextual analysis and publisher verification.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.tracking_pixel_fired_flag IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether the click tracking pixel successfully fired and recorded the event. Used for data quality validation and discrepancy troubleshooting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.user_agent IS 'The HTTP user agent string reported by the browser or application at the time of the click. Used for device detection, browser identification, and bot filtering.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: record_created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: record_updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.click_event.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE performance.delivery_pacing IS 'Real-time and near-real-time delivery pacing record tracking actual vs. planned delivery progress for each campaign line item and placement. Stores pacing period (hourly, daily), planned impression/spend target, actual delivered impressions/spend, pacing percentage, pacing status (on-pace, under-delivering, over-delivering), and recommended bid/budget adjustment signals. Sourced from Google Campaign Manager 360 and The Trade Desk pacing APIs. Critical for operational campaign management and budget stewardship.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.delivery_pacing_id IS 'Unique identifier for the delivery pacing record. Primary key for this entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.activation_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.activation. Business justification: Activation-level delivery pacing: pacing records monitor spend and impression delivery for a specific audience activation (the push of a segment to a DSP). Linking pacing to activation enables activat LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.activation.activation_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.buy_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.buy. Business justification: Delivery pacing monitors actual vs. authorized spend against executed buys. buy.authorized_spend_ceiling and buy.delivery_status are the operational targets for pacing alerts. Media ops teams run paci LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.buy.buy_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the parent campaign for which delivery pacing is being tracked. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.deliverable_tracker_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.deliverable_tracker. Business justification: Campaign delivery pacing records must reconcile against project deliverable status for campaign health reporting and client billing. Advertising ops teams routinely cross-reference actual impression/s LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.deliverable_tracker.deliverable_tracker_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.flight_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.flight. Business justification: Flight is the primary operational unit for pacing management. Delivery pacing monitors spend and impression delivery against flight budgets; pacing alerts are flight-scoped. No existing FK links deliv LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.flight.flight_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.io_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.io_line. Business justification: Pacing monitors delivery against contracted IO line commitments. Required for under-delivery alerts, budget reallocation decisions, vendor delivery performance tracking, and triggering makegood clause LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.vendor.io_line.io_line_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.line_item_id IS 'Reference to the specific campaign line item being paced. Line items represent individual media buys or placements within a campaign. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.line_item.line_item_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.media_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.media_insertion_order. Business justification: IO-level pacing is a primary operational report — pacing against media_insertion_order.authorized_spend_amount and guaranteed_impressions. delivery_pacing has contract_insertion_order_id (different do LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.media_insertion_order.media_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.media_placement_id IS 'Reference to the specific media placement being tracked for delivery pacing. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.media_placement.media_placement_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.pacing_rule_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.pacing_rule. Business justification: Pacing rules define the algorithm (even, front-loaded, custom curve) governing delivery; delivery_pacing records actual execution against those rules. Linking enables pacing rule performance auditing LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.pacing_rule.pacing_rule_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.plan_line_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.plan_line. Business justification: Plan lines define planned_impressions and planned_spend — the targets against which pacing is measured. delivery_pacing has line_item_id (campaign domain) but not plan_line_id (media domain). Plan-vs- LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.plan_line.plan_line_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.programmatic_deal_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.programmatic_deal. Business justification: Programmatic deal pacing against impression_commitment is a named DSP operational process. delivery_pacing monitors spend and impression delivery; programmatic_deal.impression_commitment is the contra LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.programmatic_deal.programmatic_deal_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.segment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.segment. Business justification: Segment-level pacing monitoring: programmatic ops teams track delivery pacing broken down by audience segment to identify which segments are over- or under-delivering against plan, enabling real-time LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.segment.segment_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.sla_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sla. Business justification: SLA breach alerting: delivery_pacing monitors real-time spend and impression delivery against plan. Linking to the governing SLA enables automated breach threshold monitoring, escalation triggering, a LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sla.sla_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.trafficking_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.trafficking_order. Business justification: Trafficking orders are the ad server instructions that drive delivery; pacing records measure whether those instructions are delivering correctly. Linking enables diagnosis of pacing issues caused by LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.trafficking_order.trafficking_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.actual_impressions IS 'The actual number of impressions delivered during this pacing period as reported by the ad server or demand-side platform (DSP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.actual_spend_amount IS 'The actual spend amount incurred during this pacing period as reported by the billing system or DSP.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.alert_severity IS 'The severity level of the pacing alert if triggered. None means no alert, low/medium/high/critical indicate escalating levels of deviation requiring intervention.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.bid_win_rate IS 'For programmatic campaigns, the percentage of bid requests that resulted in won auctions during this pacing period. Low win rates may indicate bid prices are too low.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.click_through_rate IS 'The percentage of impressions that resulted in clicks during this pacing period, calculated as (clicks / impressions) * 100. Key performance indicator for engagement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.conversion_count IS 'The total number of conversions attributed to this line item or placement during the pacing period, based on conversion tracking pixels and attribution models.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for the spend amounts (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.data_source_system IS 'The operational system from which this pacing data was sourced. Typically Google Campaign Manager 360 for direct ad serving or The Trade Desk for programmatic campaigns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.delivery_method IS 'The delivery pacing strategy configured for this line item. Standard spreads delivery evenly, accelerated delivers as fast as possible, even maintains consistent daily delivery, ASAP prioritizes immediate delivery, frontloaded concentrates delivery early in the flight.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.effective_cpa IS 'The effective cost per conversion for this pacing period, calculated as actual_spend_amount / conversion_count. Key metric for performance-based campaigns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.effective_cpm IS 'The effective cost per thousand impressions for this pacing period, calculated as (actual_spend_amount / actual_impressions) * 1000. Used to evaluate media efficiency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.frequency_cap_reached IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether the frequency cap has been reached for this line item during the pacing period, which may impact delivery velocity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.impression_pacing_percentage IS 'The percentage of planned impressions that have been delivered, calculated as (actual_impressions / planned_impressions) * 100. Values above 100 indicate over-delivery.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.inventory_availability_score IS 'A score (0-100) representing the availability of ad inventory matching the targeting criteria during this pacing period. Low scores may explain under-delivery.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.is_active IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether this pacing record represents the current active measurement period. False indicates historical or superseded records.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.measurement_timestamp IS 'The exact timestamp when this pacing measurement was captured from the source system. Critical for understanding data freshness and real-time vs near-real-time reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.notes IS 'Free-text notes from campaign managers or automated systems explaining pacing anomalies, corrective actions taken, or contextual information about delivery performance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.pacing_alert_triggered IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether an automated pacing alert was triggered for this period due to significant variance from plan, requiring campaign manager attention.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.pacing_granularity IS 'The time granularity at which pacing is measured and reported. Hourly for real-time optimization, daily for standard monitoring, weekly for longer flights, or flight for entire campaign duration.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.pacing_period_end IS 'The end timestamp of the pacing measurement period. Defines the conclusion of the window for which delivery progress is being measured.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.pacing_period_start IS 'The start timestamp of the pacing measurement period. Defines the beginning of the window for which delivery progress is being measured.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.pacing_status IS 'Current delivery pacing status indicating whether the line item or placement is delivering as planned. On-pace means within acceptable variance, under-delivering means behind target, over-delivering means ahead of target, paused means delivery is stopped, completed means flight has ended, at-risk means significant deviation detected.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.pacing_variance_threshold IS 'The acceptable variance threshold percentage used to determine pacing status. If actual pacing percentage deviates from 100% by more than this threshold, status changes from on-pace to under/over-delivering.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.planned_impressions IS 'The target number of impressions planned to be delivered during this pacing period based on the media plan and flight schedule.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.planned_spend_amount IS 'The target spend amount planned for this pacing period based on the media budget allocation and flight schedule.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.quality_score IS 'Platform-assigned quality score (typically 0-10 scale) reflecting ad relevance, landing page experience, and expected CTR. Higher scores improve auction competitiveness.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.recommended_bid_adjustment IS 'System-generated recommendation for bid adjustment to correct pacing issues. Positive values suggest increasing bids to accelerate delivery, negative values suggest decreasing bids to slow delivery.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.recommended_budget_adjustment IS 'System-generated recommendation for budget adjustment to correct pacing issues. Positive values suggest increasing budget allocation, negative values suggest reducing budget allocation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.source_record_reference IS 'The unique identifier of this pacing record in the source operational system, used for data lineage and reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.spend_pacing_percentage IS 'The percentage of planned spend that has been consumed, calculated as (actual_spend_amount / planned_spend_amount) * 100. Values above 100 indicate over-spend.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.viewability_rate IS 'The percentage of delivered impressions that met viewability standards (MRC: 50% of pixels in view for 1+ seconds for display, 2+ seconds for video) during this pacing period.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.delivery_pacing.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE performance.impression_event IS 'Raw delivery event record capturing each individual ad impression served across all channels and placements. Stores the atomic unit of campaign delivery — timestamp, placement, creative, device, geo, and auction-level signals from ad servers (Google Campaign Manager 360) and DSPs (The Trade Desk). Foundation for all downstream delivery measurement and billing reconciliation. Distinct from aggregated metrics: this is the raw event log at the impression grain.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.impression_event_id IS 'Unique identifier for each individual ad impression event. Primary key for the impression event log. Serves as the atomic unit for all downstream delivery measurement, billing reconciliation, and performance analytics.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.activation_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.activation. Business justification: Activations push audience segments to DSPs/platforms where impressions are served. Links impression delivery to the specific activation job, enables match rate analysis, activation performance measure LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.activation.activation_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.ad_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.ad. Business justification: Ad-level impression tracking drives frequency capping enforcement and creative rotation analysis. Ad ops must know which specific ad unit served each impression to validate rotation weights and freque LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.ad.ad_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the advertiser client on whose behalf this impression was served. Enables client-level reporting and cross-campaign analysis. LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.advertiser.advertiser_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.asset_id IS 'Reference to the creative asset that was displayed in this impression. Links to creative master data containing asset specifications, format, dimensions, and approval status. LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.asset.asset_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: Brand-level performance reporting is core to advertising operations. Brand managers and clients require impression delivery metrics aggregated by brand for campaign optimization, media mix analysis, a LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.client.brand.brand_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the parent advertising campaign under which this impression was served. Enables campaign-level aggregation and performance rollup. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.contract_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_insertion_order. Business justification: IO-level billing reconciliation: impression events must be reconciled against IO committed impressions for invoicing and make-good determination. click_event and conversion_event already carry this FK LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.contract_insertion_order.contract_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.flight_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.flight. Business justification: Flight-level impression reporting is essential for budget pacing and delivery reconciliation. Ad ops teams monitor impressions per flight daily to manage spend against flight budgets. No existing FK l LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.flight.flight_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.line_item_id IS 'Reference to the media plan line item or insertion order line that governs this impression delivery. Critical for pacing, budget tracking, and billing reconciliation. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.line_item.line_item_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.lookalike_model_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.lookalike_model. Business justification: Lookalike model performance reporting: when impressions are served to lookalike-expanded audiences, analysts must trace which model drove targeting to evaluate model ROI, reach accuracy, and CPM effic LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.lookalike_model.lookalike_model_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.media_placement_id IS 'Reference to the specific media placement where this impression was delivered. Links to the media placement master data defining publisher, site, position, and format. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.media_placement.media_placement_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.programmatic_deal_id IS 'The identifier for the programmatic guaranteed deal, private marketplace (PMP) deal, or preferred deal under which this impression was transacted. Links to deal master data for supply-path analysis. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.programmatic_deal.programmatic_deal_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.publisher_id IS 'Reference to the publisher or media property where the impression was delivered. Links to publisher master data for supply-side analysis and reconciliation. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.publisher.publisher_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.segment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.segment. Business justification: Core targeting relationship - every impression is served to a targeted audience segment. Essential for segment performance reporting, ROAS analysis, and optimization decisions. Fundamental to campaign LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.segment.segment_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.suppression_list_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.suppression_list. Business justification: Impressions must respect suppression lists (frequency caps, opt-outs, competitive exclusions). Critical for compliance with privacy regulations, honoring user preferences, and preventing over-exposure LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.suppression_list.suppression_list_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.trafficking_instruction_id IS 'Reference to the trafficking instruction that governed the delivery of this impression. Links to ad server trafficking configuration for delivery validation and troubleshooting. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.trafficking_instruction.trafficking_instruction_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.trafficking_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.trafficking_order. Business justification: Trafficking QA requires validating that impressions are being served under the correct trafficking order. Ad servers tag impressions with the order that served them; linking enables SLA validation (sl LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.trafficking_order.trafficking_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.ad_position IS 'The position of the ad unit on the page or within the app. Indicates placement prominence and impacts viewability and engagement rates. Code set: ref.ad_position.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.ad_server_source IS 'The ad serving platform or demand-side platform (DSP) that recorded and delivered this impression. Identifies the operational system of record for this event.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.ad_size IS 'The pixel dimensions of the ad creative served (e.g., 300x250, 728x90, 1920x1080). Used for format performance analysis and creative optimization.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.audience_segment_ids IS 'Comma-separated list of audience segment IDs that the user matched at impression time. Links to audience taxonomy from DMP (Data Management Platform) or CDP (Customer Data Platform). Used for audience targeting validation and performance analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.bid_price_cpm IS 'The winning bid price for this impression expressed in CPM (Cost Per Mille / cost per thousand impressions). Represents the clearing price in the programmatic auction. Used for media cost analysis and ROAS calculation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.brand_safety_score IS 'A score from 0.00 to 100.00 indicating the brand safety level of the content context where the impression was served. Higher scores indicate safer, more brand-appropriate environments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.browser IS 'The web browser or app environment in which the impression was displayed (e.g., Chrome, Safari, Firefox, in-app). Used for browser-specific performance and compatibility analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.channel IS 'The digital channel or device environment where the impression was delivered. Includes desktop web, mobile web, mobile app, Connected TV (CTV), Over-the-Top (OTT), and Digital Out-of-Home (DOOH).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.consent_status IS 'Indicates whether user consent was obtained for data collection and ad personalization at impression time. Critical for GDPR and CCPA compliance. Values: granted (consent obtained), denied (consent refused), not_required (jurisdiction does not require consent), unknown (consent status not captured).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.content_category IS 'The IAB content category or taxonomy classification of the page or app content where the impression was served. Used for contextual targeting validation and brand safety analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for the media cost and bid price. Enables multi-currency campaign analysis and financial reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.device_type IS 'The category of device on which the impression was rendered. Used for device-level performance analysis and cross-device attribution. Code set: ref.device_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.event_source_system IS 'The name and version of the source system that generated this impression event record. Used for data lineage tracking and cross-system reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.fraud_score IS 'A risk score from 0.00 to 100.00 indicating the likelihood that this impression is fraudulent or invalid. Generated by fraud detection vendors or internal algorithms. Higher scores indicate higher fraud risk.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.frequency_cap_count IS 'The number of times this user has been exposed to this campaign or creative prior to this impression. Used for frequency capping enforcement and ad fatigue analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.geo_city IS 'The city or designated market area (DMA) where the impression was delivered. Enables hyper-local targeting validation and metro-level performance analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.geo_country_code IS 'Three-letter ISO country code representing the geographic location where the impression was delivered. Derived from IP geolocation or device GPS. Used for geo-targeting validation and regional performance analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.geo_postal_code IS 'The postal or ZIP code where the impression was delivered. Supports neighborhood-level targeting and local market analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.geo_region IS 'The state, province, or region where the impression was delivered. Supports sub-national geographic analysis and local market performance tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.impression_timestamp IS 'Exact date and time when the ad impression was served to the end user. Represents the real-world event time of ad delivery. Critical for time-series analysis, dayparting optimization, and billing reconciliation. Format: yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ss.SSSXXX.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.impression_type IS 'The format or modality of the ad impression served. Distinguishes between display banners, video ads, native content, audio spots, and rich media executions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.ingestion_timestamp IS 'The timestamp when this impression event record was ingested into the lakehouse silver layer. Used for data freshness monitoring and ETL (Extract Transform Load) pipeline auditing. Format: yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ss.SSSXXX.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.ip_address IS 'The IP address of the device that received the impression. Used for geo-targeting validation, fraud detection, and audience verification. May be considered PII under GDPR and CCPA.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.is_autoplay IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether the video ad started playing automatically without user initiation. Applicable to video impressions. Impacts user experience and engagement metrics.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.is_bot_traffic IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether the impression was identified as non-human bot traffic. Used for invalid traffic (IVT) filtering and billing adjustment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.is_muted IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether the video or audio ad was muted at the time of impression. Applicable to video and audio impression types. Impacts engagement and completion rates.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.latitude IS 'The latitude coordinate of the impression delivery location. Used for proximity-based targeting validation and location-based analytics, particularly for DOOH and mobile campaigns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.longitude IS 'The longitude coordinate of the impression delivery location. Used for proximity-based targeting validation and location-based analytics, particularly for DOOH and mobile campaigns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.media_cost IS 'The actual media cost incurred for this single impression. Calculated from the bid price or rate card. Used for billing reconciliation, budget tracking, and ROI (Return on Investment) analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.operating_system IS 'The operating system of the device that rendered the impression (e.g., iOS, Android, Windows, macOS). Supports device compatibility analysis and targeting optimization.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.page_url IS 'The full URL of the page where the impression was displayed. Supports contextual analysis, brand safety verification, and content alignment validation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.session_code IS 'The unique identifier for the user session during which this impression was served. Enables session-level analysis and cross-impression journey tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.site_domain IS 'The domain name of the website or app where the impression was served. Used for brand safety analysis, contextual targeting validation, and publisher performance tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.supply_chain_object IS 'The sellers.json or SupplyChain object captured at impression time, identifying all intermediaries in the programmatic supply chain. Used for supply-path transparency and optimization per IAB ads.txt and sellers.json standards.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.tcf_consent_string IS 'The IAB Transparency and Consent Framework (TCF) consent string captured at impression time. Encodes user consent choices for data processing purposes. Required for GDPR compliance in programmatic advertising.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.time_in_view_seconds IS 'The total duration in seconds that the impression was visible in the users viewport. Critical metric for engagement analysis and viewability quality assessment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.user_agent IS 'The full user agent string captured at impression time. Contains detailed device, browser, and operating system information for advanced device fingerprinting and fraud detection.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.user_identifier IS 'The pseudonymized or hashed user identifier (cookie ID, device ID, or universal ID) associated with this impression. Used for cross-device tracking, frequency management, and attribution. Subject to GDPR and CCPA privacy regulations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.video_duration_seconds IS 'The total duration of the video ad creative in seconds. Applicable only to video impression types. Used for video completion rate analysis and engagement measurement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.video_player_size IS 'The size category of the video player at impression time. Applicable to video impressions. Impacts viewability and user engagement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.viewability_percentage IS 'The percentage of the ad creative that was visible in the viewport at the time of measurement. Ranges from 0.00 to 100.00. Used for granular viewability analysis and quality scoring.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.viewability_status IS 'Indicates whether the impression met the MRC (Media Rating Council) viewability standard at the time of delivery. Viewable means the ad was in-view per IAB/MRC guidelines (50% of pixels visible for 1+ seconds for display, 2+ seconds for video).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.impression_event.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE performance.video_completion_event IS 'Video ad completion event record capturing quartile-level video engagement signals (25%, 50%, 75%, 100% completion) per video ad impression. Stores video ad unit identifier, completion quartile reached, autoplay flag, sound-on flag, skip action (skipped, completed), player size, and VTR (View-Through Rate) computation inputs. Sourced from VAST/VPAID event signals from video ad servers. Supports VTR-based IO commitments and video campaign performance measurement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.video_completion_event_id IS 'Unique identifier for the video completion event record. Primary key for this event log entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.ad_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.ad. Business justification: Ad-level video completion tracking is essential for creative performance analysis. Creative teams compare completion_quartile distributions across ad variants to identify which video creative lengths LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.ad.ad_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.asset_id IS 'Identifier of the video creative asset that was played. Links to the specific video ad unit served. LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.asset.asset_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.buy_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.buy. Business justification: Video buys often carry completion rate guarantees; makegood eligibility is assessed by comparing video_completion_event data against buy-level commitments. video_completion_event has media_placement_i LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.buy.buy_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.campaign_id IS 'Identifier of the advertising campaign this video completion event belongs to. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.flight_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.flight. Business justification: Flight-level video completion rate (VCR) is a standard video campaign KPI used for pacing and creative optimization. Video buyers evaluate VCR per flight to determine whether video creative is resonat LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.flight.flight_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.impression_event_id IS 'Identifier linking this completion event to the parent video ad impression that was served. References the initial ad serving event. LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.impression_event.impression_event_id (not enforced: partitioned target).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.line_item_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.line_item. Business justification: Line-item VCR is a standard programmatic video optimization metric. Traders use line-item completion rates to adjust bids and targeting for video line items. No existing FK links video_completion_even LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.line_item.line_item_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.media_placement_id IS 'Identifier of the media placement where this video ad was served. Links to the specific inventory position purchased. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.media_placement.media_placement_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.programmatic_deal_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.programmatic_deal. Business justification: Programmatic video deals carry completion rate commitments. Deal-level video completion reporting (quartile rates, skip rates) is a standard DSP/publisher reconciliation report. video_completion_event LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.programmatic_deal.programmatic_deal_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.publisher_id IS 'Identifier of the publisher or content owner on whose property the video ad was served. Links to the supply-side partner. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.publisher.publisher_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.spec_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.spec. Business justification: Video completion rates are analyzed by spec (15s vs 30s, skippable vs non-skippable). Linking video_completion_event to spec enables spec-level completion rate benchmarking — a standard creative optim LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.spec.spec_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.ad_server IS 'Name of the ad server platform that served the video ad and captured this completion event (e.g., Google Campaign Manager 360, Innovid, Sizmek). Used for data quality and discrepancy analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.browser IS 'Web browser or app environment where the video ad was served (e.g., Chrome, Safari, Firefox, in-app). Null for CTV (Connected TV) and OTT (Over-the-Top) environments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.completion_percentage IS 'Percentage of the video that was viewed, calculated as (time_to_completion_seconds / video_duration_seconds) * 100. Supports VTR (View-Through Rate) calculation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.completion_quartile IS 'The quartile milestone reached in video playback: start (0%), first_quartile (25%), midpoint (50%), third_quartile (75%), or complete (100%). Used to calculate VTR (View-Through Rate) and engagement depth.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.connection_type IS 'Type of network connection used during video playback: wifi, cellular (3G/4G/5G), wired (ethernet), or unknown. Impacts video quality and completion rates.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.content_category IS 'IAB Content Taxonomy category of the content adjacent to the video ad (e.g., Sports, News, Entertainment). Used for contextual targeting and brand safety verification.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.device_type IS 'Type of device on which the video ad was viewed: desktop, mobile (smartphone), tablet, CTV (Connected TV), console (gaming console), or other. Critical for cross-device campaign analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.event_timestamp IS 'Precise date and time when the video completion event was captured by the ad server or video player, in ISO 8601 format (yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ss.SSSXXX).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.geo_city IS 'City where the video ad was viewed. Used for hyper-local campaign performance analysis and geo-targeting verification.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.geo_country_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 country code where the video ad was viewed (e.g., USA, GBR, CAN). Used for geo-targeting verification and regional performance analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.geo_region IS 'State, province, or region where the video ad was viewed (e.g., California, Ontario, Bavaria). Used for sub-national geo-targeting analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.ip_address_hashed IS 'Hashed IP address of the device that viewed the video ad. Used for fraud detection and geo-verification while maintaining privacy compliance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.is_autoplay IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether the video ad started playing automatically without user initiation (True) or required user action to start (False). Impacts viewability and engagement quality.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.is_fullscreen IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether the video was playing in fullscreen mode at the time of the completion event (True) or in standard embedded player (False).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.is_skipped IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether the user actively skipped the video ad before completion (True) or allowed it to play through the recorded quartile (False).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.is_sound_on IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether the video ad played with sound enabled (True) or muted (False). Critical metric for video engagement quality and IO (Insertion Order) compliance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.is_viewable IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether the video ad met MRC (Media Rating Council) viewability standards at the time of the completion event: 50% of pixels in-view for 2+ consecutive seconds. Used for viewable VTR (View-Through Rate) calculation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.operating_system IS 'Operating system of the device where the video ad was viewed (e.g., iOS, Android, Windows, macOS, tvOS, Roku OS). Used for device-level performance segmentation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.player_height_pixels IS 'Height of the video player in pixels at the time of the completion event. Used for precise viewability and player size analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.player_size IS 'Size classification of the video player at the time of the event: small (<400x300), medium (400x300 to 640x480), large (>640x480 but not fullscreen), or fullscreen. Impacts viewability measurement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.player_width_pixels IS 'Width of the video player in pixels at the time of the completion event. Used for precise viewability and player size analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.session_code IS 'Identifier for the user browsing or viewing session during which this video completion event occurred. Used for session-level engagement analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.site_domain IS 'Domain name of the website or app where the video ad was served (e.g., youtube.com, espn.com). Used for brand safety and contextual analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.skip_offset_seconds IS 'Number of seconds into the video when the skip button became available to the user. Null if video was non-skippable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.time_to_completion_seconds IS 'Actual elapsed time in seconds from video start to the recorded completion quartile. May differ from video_duration_seconds if user paused, rewound, or fast-forwarded.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.user_id_hashed IS 'Hashed or pseudonymized identifier for the user who viewed the video ad. Used for frequency capping and cross-device attribution while maintaining privacy compliance. Must comply with GDPR (General Data Protection Regulation) and CCPA (California Consumer Privacy Act).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.vast_version IS 'Version of the VAST (Video Ad Serving Template) specification used to serve this video ad (e.g., 2.0, 3.0, 4.0, 4.1, 4.2). Indicates ad serving protocol capabilities and tracking fidelity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.video_duration_seconds IS 'Total duration of the video creative in seconds. Used to calculate completion percentage and time-based engagement metrics.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.video_format IS 'Format type of the video ad: linear (pre-roll, mid-roll, post-roll that interrupts content), non_linear (overlay ads that run concurrently with content), or companion (static/rich media ads displayed alongside video).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.video_position IS 'Position of the video ad within the content stream: pre_roll (before content), mid_roll (during content), or post_roll (after content). Applies to linear video formats only.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.viewable_percentage IS 'Percentage of the video player that was in the viewable area of the browser viewport at the time of the completion event. Used for granular viewability analysis beyond binary MRC threshold.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.vpaid_version IS 'Version of the VPAID (Video Player-Ad Interface Definition) specification used for interactive video ads (e.g., 1.0, 2.0). Null for standard VAST-only video ads.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.video_completion_event.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE performance.viewability_measurement IS 'Viewability measurement record per impression or placement-day, capturing MRC-compliant viewability signals: in-view percentage, time-in-view (seconds), viewable impression count, measurable impression count, and viewability rate. Sourced from third-party measurement vendors (Comscore, IAS, DoubleVerify) and ad server signals. Supports viewability-guaranteed IO commitments and brand safety compliance reporting per MRC and IAB standards.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.viewability_measurement_id IS 'Unique identifier for the viewability measurement record. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.asset_id IS 'Reference to the creative asset that was served and measured for viewability. LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.asset.asset_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.buy_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.buy. Business justification: Viewability guarantees are contracted at the buy level (guaranteed_viewability buys). viewability_measurement results must be reconciled against the buy to verify contractual compliance and trigger ma LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.buy.buy_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the advertising campaign associated with this viewability measurement. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.flight_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.flight. Business justification: Flight-level viewability reporting validates IO commitments scoped to specific flight windows. Guaranteed viewability IOs are often structured per flight; viewability_guaranteed_io_flag on this table LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.flight.flight_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.impression_event_id IS 'Unique identifier for the individual ad impression being measured. Links to ad server impression logs. LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.impression_event.impression_event_id (not enforced: partitioned target).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.line_item_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.line_item. Business justification: Line-item viewability tracking is required for contractual compliance on guaranteed viewability buys. Ad ops teams report viewability_rate per line_item against viewability_target_percentage on the li LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.line_item.line_item_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.media_placement_id IS 'Reference to the media placement being measured for viewability. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.media_placement.media_placement_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.programmatic_deal_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.programmatic_deal. Business justification: Programmatic deals specify viewability_threshold_pct as a contractual term. Deal health dashboards compare viewability_measurement.viewability_rate against programmatic_deal.viewability_threshold_pct. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.programmatic_deal.programmatic_deal_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.publisher_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.publisher. Business justification: Publisher-level viewability rate reporting is a core ad ops and vendor scorecard function. viewability_measurement already has supplier_id (measurement vendor) but lacks publisher_id (inventory owner) LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.publisher.publisher_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.sla_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sla. Business justification: Viewability SLAs are common contractual guarantees in media agreements. Direct link enables automated compliance monitoring, breach detection, penalty calculation, and make-good triggering. Core to co LOGICAL REF -> crm_db.contract.sla.sla_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.spec_id IS 'Foreign key linking to creative.spec. Business justification: Viewability measurement is validated against the ad spec''s dimensions and IAB standard unit. Spec defines guaranteed_viewability_threshold context; linking enables spec-level viewability compliance re LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.spec.spec_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Viewability measurements are provided by third-party verification vendors (IAS, MOAT, DoubleVerify). Agencies need FK to supplier for vendor performance scorecards, contract compliance tracking, discr LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.ad_format IS 'The format type of the ad unit being measured (display, video, native, rich media, interstitial, expandable).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.audible_on_complete_flag IS 'For video ads, indicates whether the ad was audible when the video completed. Supports audible and viewable measurement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.brand_safety_flag IS 'Indicates whether the placement passed brand safety verification at the time of viewability measurement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.data_quality_score IS 'A quality score (0-100) assigned by the measurement vendor indicating the reliability and accuracy of the viewability measurement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.device_type IS 'The type of device on which the ad was served and measured (desktop, mobile, tablet, CTV, OTT, DOOH).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.environment IS 'The digital environment where the ad was served (web browser, in-app, CTV, DOOH).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.guaranteed_viewability_threshold IS 'The contractual viewability rate threshold (percentage) guaranteed in the insertion order, if applicable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.in_view_percentage IS 'The percentage of the ad creative pixels that were visible in the viewport at the time of measurement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.invalid_traffic_flag IS 'Indicates whether the impression was flagged as invalid traffic (bot, fraud, or non-human traffic) by the measurement vendor.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.measurability_rate IS 'The percentage of total impressions that were measurable for viewability, calculated as (measurable_impression_count / total_impression_count) * 100.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.measurable_impression_count IS 'The total number of impressions for which viewability could be measured (excludes unmeasurable impressions due to technical limitations).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.measurement_date IS 'The calendar date of the viewability measurement, used for daily aggregation and reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.measurement_method IS 'The technical methodology used to measure viewability (geometric, browser optimization, or reach extension).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.measurement_status IS 'The current status of the viewability measurement record (measured, unmeasurable, pending, error).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.measurement_timestamp IS 'The exact date and time when the viewability measurement was captured. Principal business event timestamp for this measurement record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.mrc_compliant_flag IS 'Indicates whether this viewability measurement meets MRC accreditation standards and methodology requirements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.player_size_height IS 'The height of the video player or ad container in pixels at the time of measurement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.player_size_width IS 'The width of the video player or ad container in pixels at the time of measurement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.source_system IS 'The operational system or platform that originated this viewability measurement record (e.g., Google Campaign Manager 360, Comscore, The Trade Desk).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.time_in_view_seconds IS 'The total duration in seconds that the ad was in-view (meeting the pixel threshold) during the measurement window.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.total_impression_count IS 'The total number of ad impressions served, including both measurable and unmeasurable impressions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.unmeasurable_reason IS 'The reason why viewability could not be measured for this impression (e.g., cross-domain iframe, ad blocker, technical limitation).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.video_quartile_reached IS 'For video ads, the furthest quartile reached while the ad was viewable (0%, 25%, 50%, 75%, 100%). Not applicable for non-video formats.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.viewability_guaranteed_io_flag IS 'Indicates whether this impression is part of a viewability-guaranteed insertion order commitment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.viewability_rate IS 'The percentage of measurable impressions that were viewable, calculated as (viewable_impression_count / measurable_impression_count) * 100.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.viewability_standard IS 'The viewability standard applied for this measurement (MRC display: 50%/1s, MRC video: 50%/2s, GroupM, or custom client standard).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.viewable_impression_count IS 'The number of impressions that met the MRC viewability standard (50% of pixels in-view for 1 second for display, 2 seconds for video).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN performance.viewability_measurement.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';
